\cf3\ul\b N\ulnone o disassembly\cf0\b0  toggles the start of the disassembly process. If "No disassembly" is checked, the disassembly process only takes place when a binary file is loaded. If this option is not checked (this is the default), disassembly is done each time a byte type is set or each time Assembler format is changed. Checking this menu is usefull when you need to do many changes without being disturbed by the disassembly process.\par
\par
