\cf1\ul\b\f1\fs32 Setting Type To Bytes\par
\cf0\f2\par
\ulnone\b0\f0\fs24 As we said earlier, \b DISASSEMBLY is an INTERACTIVE and ITERATIVE PROCESS\b0 . This chapter explains how this is achieved by DIS6502.\par
\par
You can improve the disassembly process by looking at the dump and changing the byte type. \b Each byte of the object file has an associated type given by DIS6502.\b0  At first, all the bytes are considered as CODE so the disassembler tries to disassemble all bytes of the file as if they were code.\par
\par
You can change the byte type by selecting some bytes in the dump window and clicking with the right button. A popup menu will appear. Choose 'Type' and a sub-menu will appear. Then you can select the new type for the selection.\par
