\f0 DIS6502 will disassemble again the file but this time the text "Setting Up ATARI 130XE Ram Disk..." appears in \b .BYTE directives\b0  and not as 6502 instructions (AND #$7D, ORA L1D1D,X...).\par
\par
The different types are:\par
\par
\pard{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf7\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\cf2\ul Code\cf0\ulnone , \par
\cf2\ul{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Code with Low Byte\cf0\ulnone , \par
\cf2\ul{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Code with High Byte\cf0\ulnone , \par
\cf2\ul{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Byte\cf0\ulnone , \par
