\pard{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf7\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\cf3\b .END\cf0\b0  \par
\pard\li720\par
This is the complete syntax to end a disassembly listing. Enter the name of the directive for your assembler. Some assemblers need the name of the source file name after this directive: .END D:TEST.ASM In this case, you should check the 'Add filename' checkbox.\par
\par
Default: .END\par
\par
\pard{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf7\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\cf3\b .DS allowed\cf0\b0  \par
