\cf2\b\fs28 Include files section\par
\cf0\par
\pard{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf7\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\cf3\fs24 .INCLUDE\cf0\b0  \par
\pard\li720\par
This option defines the syntax used to include a file. This becomes important when you have a large source file. In this case, you split the file into several ones and link them with this directive. To support all the syntaxes for this directive, you have 2 fields in this option. The first one is the string that will appear BEFORE the filename. The second one is the string that will appear AFTER the filename.\par
\par
Default: .INCLUDE #\par
\par
\pard{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf7\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\cf3\b Number of lines per include file.\cf0\b0  \par
\pard\li720\par
You can set the maximum number of source lines to put in a source file. This is to prevent the disassembler from generating large source files that your editor can not load into memory.\par
\par
Default: 500\par
\par
\pard{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf7\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\cf3\b Inclusion method\cf0\b0  \par
\pard\li720\par
There are 2 ways for including files.\par
The first one makes a main source file that includes all other files.\par
\par
The second one is to include the next file at the end of each source file. Click on the method that your assembler accepts.\par
\par
Default: All files included in 1 main file\par
\par
\pard{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf7\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\cf3\b Include files allowed.\cf0\b0  \par
\pard\li720\par
Click this check box if your assembler supports include files AND if you wish to generate multiple files for your source.\par
\par
Default: ON\par
